    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Strategy---Operations-Manager--Micro---Immun_JR-017658": {
      "title": "Strategy & Operations Manager, Micro & Immun",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Continuing Faculty:  Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences Department/School:  Department of Microbiology and Immunology, School of Biomedical Sciences Salary:  Senior Manager 1 salary package, including up to 17% super  Premier and high-performing department / Apply your operational leadership to enable globally impactful medical discoveries / Collaborate with broad networks and stakeholders An opportunity to work through large and exciting projects. Investing in you - benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.    The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website.   Your responsibilities will include:   Lead integrated operational management across administration, research services and teaching support for the Department of Microbiology and Immunology. Working closely with the Head of Department, develop and implement strategic and operational plans, performance measures and resource models aligned with School and Faculty priorities. Oversee budgeting, financial monitoring and modelling, providing timely advice to the Head of Department and School Manager regarding interventions to manage risk and support decision-making for optimal outcomes. Manage infrastructure, space planning and laboratory-related operational matters, including supporting a major new building’s operational readiness. Build strong relationships across the School, Faculty, Doherty Institute and shared services to coordinate collaborative, compliant service delivery.   You may be a great fit if you:   Hold postgraduate qualifications, or significant equivalent experience, gained in large, complex organisations or research-intensive environments. Demonstrate proven operational leadership in laboratory-based, medical research, hospital or tertiary education settings. Bring extensive financial management capability, including budgeting, forecasting, modelling and advising on resource allocation and risk. Manage infrastructure, space planning and laboratory operations issues, negotiating practical, compliant solutions with diverse stakeholders. Lead inclusive, collaborative teams, creating positive, imaginative cultures that enhance both staff and student experiences. Navigate change confidently, balancing strategy and hands-on delivery while building trust across complex stakeholder networks.   For further information please refer to the attached Candidate Information Pack .   What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfillment, including:  Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being. Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance. Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance. Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program.   For more information check out our benefits page!    Your new team The Department of Microbiology and Immunology is a large, high-performing department within the School of Biomedical Sciences. Located in the southern hemisphere’s leading biomedical precinct, the School brings together scientists, clinicians and educators. You will join a collaborative culture that shares ideas, infrastructure and expertise to deliver impactful research and education.   Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.   Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team, Korin Korin, at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .   Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume, a cover letter outlining your interest and experience, and the responses against the Selection Criteria^ (found in the Position Description) as part of the application process.   ^For information to help you with compiling short statements to answer the selection criteria and competencies, please go to http://about.unimelb.edu.au/careers/selection-criteria   Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, please follow the details listed on the Position Description. For questions related to our recruitment process email Emily Haagensen at snr-talentacq@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Emily Haagensen on +61428005853 or at snr-talentacq@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').   Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future.   Applications close: 20 September 2026 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:   Candidate Information Pack - JR-017658 Strategy &amp;amp; Operations Manager, Micro and Immu.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Lecturer-in-Game-Design_JR-016132-1": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Game Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full-time; Continuing Faculty: Architecture, Building and Planning School:  Melbourne School of Design Salary: Level B - $124,656 - $148,023 p.a. plus 17% super  Develop and teach into a new Game Design major / collaborate across leading built environment disciplines / grow impactful creative practice Join us to shape game design education, mentoring diverse creatives and advancing practice-led research in interactive worlds.  Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.    The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity   In this role, you will shape a new Game Design major within the Bachelor of Design. You will lead studio teaching that connects interactive worlds with architecture, landscape, urbanism and interior design. You will grow a research or creative practice while mentoring diverse students in a collaborative, multidisciplinary faculty. What you will deliver:   Lead studio-based teaching in the Game Design major, focusing on Unreal Engine, game mechanics and level design. Design and coordinate an introductory Game Design subject that builds foundational skills in systems, interaction and player experience. Contribute to curriculum innovation, assessment design and continuous improvement of student-centred, inclusive game design pedagogy. Develop a research or creative practice profile in contemporary game design, interactive media and related design disciplines. Build industry and community partnerships, mentoring students towards professional practice through showcases, festivals, playtesting and exhibitions. You may be a great fit if you:   Hold a PhD in design or related field, or equivalent professional and creative achievements. Demonstrate tertiary teaching experience in game design or related areas, with strong studio-based, student-centred practice. Bring a developing research or creative practice profile in contemporary game design, interactive media or game studies. Offer advanced Unreal Engine skills, including Blueprints visual scripting for prototyping, interaction, systems and player experience. Experience with C++ programming and familiarity with game engines beyond Unreal Engine would be highly regarded, particularly where this demonstrates an ability to transfer technical knowledge and development practices across platforms. Apply deep expertise in level design, spatial thinking, environmental storytelling, playtesting and iterative refinement processes. Contribute to curriculum development and cross-disciplinary collaboration, with strong commitment to inclusive, equitable game design education. For further information please refer to the attached PD.  What we offer you!   We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:  Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being  Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company  Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program  For more information check out our benefits page!  Your new team You will join the Faculty of Architecture, Building and Planning, a global leader in design education. Our multidisciplinary Melbourne School of Design connects architecture, landscape, urbanism and emerging design disciplines, including game design. You will collaborate with imaginative colleagues in world-building, interactive media and spatial design, within a supportive, collegiate culture. We value diversity, creative experimentation and practice-based inquiry, offering strong mentoring, facilities and research training opportunities. Be Yourself   The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants   We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For questions related to our recruitment process email Brett Verity at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Position Description JR-016132 Lecturer in Game Design PD.docx JR-016132 Lecturer in Game Design PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Senior-Financial-Accountant--Research-_JR-016965-1": {
      "title": "Senior Financial Accountant (Research)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:   Full time ;   C ontinuing     Department :  Office of the DVC Research     Salary:   UOM7 -   $ 1 11 , 275   - $1 20 , 453   p.a.   plus   17% super     Influential research finance specialist role / ensure compliant, transparent use of external funding / mentor and uplift accounting practice   Bring your advanced accounting   expertise   to strengthen research impact and apply now to shape trusted funding stewardship.   Investing in   you   – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.    The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity     You will lead acquittals and audit reporting that ensure research funding is compliant,   transparent   and trusted.   You will mentor colleagues and collaborate with Faculties to optimise project finance management across diverse funding schemes.   What   you will   deliver :     Provide guidance,   training   and day-to-day oversight to Financial Accountant   (Research) within the team.   Working closely with the   External Research Assurance and Reporting lead   and the Senior Manager   on budgets and forecast s   Take the lead on institutional audits such as Uniform Guidance, and HERDC   Lead   timely   preparation, reconciliation and submission of research funding acquittals and audit reports to required standards   for more complex submissions .   Interpret complex funding agreements,   policies   and scheme rules to ensure   accurate   accounting and compliant financial reporting.   Partner with Grants & Contracts and Faculty stakeholders to improve project   financial management   practices and governance.   Champion continuous improvement by reviewing processes,   identifying   optimisation   opportunities   and supporting innovation in Research Finance.   You may   be a great fit   if :    Hold a relevant business degree and CA,   CPA   or equivalent formal accounting qualification.   Bring substantial experience in multi-source reconciliations, variance resolution, financial statements,   acquittals   and audit processes.   Demonstrate advanced Excel and financial modelling skills, with strength interpreting complex data for diverse stakeholders.   Communicate complex financial information clearly to clients with limited accounting knowledge, building strong working relationships.   Operate independently while coordinating team efforts, showing sound judgement,   flexibility   and comfort in evolving environments.   Contribute to high-performance cultures and engage in process mapping,   review   and reengineering for continuous improvement.     For further information please refer to the attached PD.    What we offer you!     We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of   fulfilment , including:     Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance  and well-being , including   leading parental leave,   gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance , and access to un ique cultural and recreational benefits such as   discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company     Health and   well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program     For more information check out our benefits page!     Your new team – “ Research Finance ”     Research Finance sits within Research, Innovation and   Commercialisation , a specialist team enabling the University’s research mission.   You will join a collaborative group that provides end-to-end financial support across the research project lifecycle.   The team values service excellence, big-picture thinking, attention to   detail   and creating a positive, supportive workplace.   Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at   UniMelb .   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians .   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about   our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.            Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au     Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more   about the process , including tips and FAQs .   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.     A   Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and   reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience   as part of the application process .      Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact   Connie Killey   at   connie.killey@unimelb.edu.au     For questions related to our recruitment process email  Alessandro Storani at alessandro.storani@unimleb.edu.au     For recruitment adjustments contact   Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218   or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Apply   today ,   and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.     Applications close:   ​ Sunday 13 September 2026 - 11:55 PM ;   Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:     PD_JR-016965 Senior Financial Accountant (Research).pdf PD_JR-016965 Senior Financial Accountant (Research).docx"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Senior-Research-Finance-Partnering-Lead_JR-016946-1": {
      "title": "Senior Research Finance Partnering Lead",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:   Full Time; Continuing   Department:   Research, Innovation and   Commercialisation   (RIC)   Salary:   UoM 9 - $146,049 - $151,951   plus 17% super   Senior leadership in research finance / shape shared services innovation / enable world-class research impact   Apply now to lead research finance partnering and support transformative, externally funded projects across the University.   Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.      The University of Melbourne   We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity     In this senior partnering role, you will lead research finance operations for a major Faculty cluster. You will guide researchers through complex funding rules while driving innovation in shared services processes and systems.   What you will deliver:     Maintain trusted advisory relationships with senior researchers and Faculty leaders on budgeting,   forecasting   and research   financial management .   Lead and coach Research Finance Partnering staff, fostering high performance, continuous   improvement   and strong client service.   Coordinate day-to-day research finance operations,   optimising   resource allocation, processes, and enabling technologies across the team.   Provide   specialist faculty-level research finance advice, including reporting,   forecasting   and budgeting for complex project portfolios.   Contribute to continuous improvement of people, processes,   systems   and performance within the finance shared services model.   You may be a great fit if you:     Hold a relevant business degree plus CA,   CPA   or equivalent professional accounting qualification.   Bring extensive experience managing research funding from multiple agencies, ensuring compliance and sector best practice.   Lead professional finance teams, applying contemporary leadership, coaching and performance management to build capability.   Demonstrate strong financial modelling skills and the ability to interpret complex data for senior stakeholders.   Adapt effectively within complex matrix structures, championing business improvement   initiatives   and continuous process enhancement.   Manage diverse stakeholders with excellent   organisational   skills,   prioritising   competing deadlines while delivering responsive client service.   For further information, please refer to the attached PD.     What we offer you!     We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:    Build future financial security with 17% superannuation   Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being    Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning   Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave   Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company    Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program    For more information check out our benefits page!     Your new team   Research Finance sits within Research, Innovation and   Commercialisation , enabling the University’s research and innovation mission. We provide end-to-end financial support across thousands of externally funded projects, ensuring compliance and transparent reporting to funders. Our team collaborates closely with academic leaders, business development   experts   and operational finance colleagues across all divisions. We value service excellence, big-picture   thinking   and attention to detail, creating an innovative, supportive environment for professionals.   Joining us, you contribute directly to world-class research impact while growing your leadership and technical   expertise .   Be Yourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe   organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.     Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with Korin   Korin , our Indigenous Employment and Development team, via   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au   Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.    A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your   resume and a cover letter   outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.   Please upload a   separate document addressing the Selection Criteria   outlined in the Position Description.     Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact Connie Killey via email at   connie.killey@unimelb.edu.au     For questions related to our recruitment process email Alessandro Storani at alessandro.storani@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').    Apply   today, and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.   Applications close:   Sunday 13 September at   11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.    Position Description:   JR-016946 Senior Research Finance Partnering Lead -PD.docx JR-016946 Senior Research Finance Partnering Lead -PD.pdf"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville/Health-Informatics-Specialist_JR-015969": {
      "title": "Health Informatics Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type: Full Time; Fixed Term for 2 years Faculty: Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences Department / School:  Department of Infectious Diseases Salary: $152,695 - $176,065 p.a. (pro-rate for part time) plus 17% super Pivotal informatics role in pandemic therapeutics / shape secure global health data sharing / partner with clinicians, researchers and governments Apply your health informatics expertise to build trusted data pipelines that accelerate pandemic therapeutics discovery and translation. Investing in you – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities. The University of Melbourne We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to benefit society through the transformative impact of education and research. Discover more via our website. Your next career opportunity In this Health Informatician role, you will lead secure health data sharing for pandemic therapeutics research with the Cummings Global Centre for Pandemic Therapeutics (CGCPT). You will design robust governance, analytics and infrastructure that connect hospitals, laboratories, governments and global collaborators. You will gain wide exposure to senior stakeholders and cutting-edge infectious diseases science at the Doherty Institute and the Melbourne biomedical precinct. What you will deliver: Lead development and implementation of data governance frameworks, agreements and policies for CGCPT health data assets. Establish and manage efficient workflows for secure data sharing with hospitals, laboratories, governments and international partners. Collaborate with computational scientists and software engineers to deliver fit-for-purpose databases and data repository infrastructure. Support data-driven research projects and competitive grant applications through expert advice on data design, access and analysis. Design and deliver training for CGCPT staff and students on best practice in health data sharing and governance. You may be a great fit if you: Lead development and implementation of data governance frameworks, agreements and policies for CGCPT health data assets. Establish and manage efficient workflows for secure data sharing with hospitals, laboratories, governments and international partners. Collaborate with computational scientists and engineers to deliver fit-for-purpose databases and data repository infrastructure. Support data-driven research projects and competitive grant applications through expert advice on data design, access and analysis. Design and deliver training for CGCPT staff and students on best practice in health data sharing and governance. For further information, please refer to the attached PD. What we offer you! We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including: Build future financial security with 17% superannuation Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program For more information check out our benefits page! Your new team - The Department of Infectious Diseases at the Doherty Institute unites leading experts in infectious diseases, immunity and public health from across Melbourne and beyond. The Cummings Global Centre for Pandemic Therapeutics (CGCPT) pioneers innovative pandemic therapeutics with strong clinical and translational partnerships. The Computational Sciences Initiative drives advanced analytics, informatics and data platforms that power high-impact, collaborative research. You will join an inclusive, mission-driven community that values innovation, teamwork, professional growth and real-world health impact. Be Yourself The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe organisation. The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences. Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb. We're committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities. Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process. Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit our Indigenous staff page to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.    Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au . Application essentials: Visit \"apply with us\" to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs. You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role. A Working with Children Check is required for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you. Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process. Please upload your responses to the Selection Criteria, found in the Position Description. Want to know more? For queries related to this specific position, contact A/Prof David Price at david.price1@unimelb.edu.au For questions related to our recruitment process email Walid at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments'). Apply today, and join a community that’s shaping the future. Applications close: 11 September 2026 11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone. Position Description: JR-015969 Health Informatics Specialist PD.docx JR-015969 Health Informatics Specialist PD.pdf"
    },
