    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Casual-Academics---Melbourne-Dental-School_JR-017697-1": {
      "title": "Casual Academics - Melbourne Dental School",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-21\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nVariable time\n\nRole type:   Casual; Sessional academic   Faculty:   Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences   Department / School:   Melbourne Dental School   Salary:   Casual   sessional   academic rates as per University of Melbourne Enterprise Agreement, plus   1 2 % super     Shape the next generation of   oral health practitioners by   teaching    in   the   D octor of Dental Surgery (D DS ) ,   Bachelor of Oral Health ( BOH ) , and Doctor of Clinical Dentistry (DCD)   program s   at   Melbourne Dental   School   / Enjoy flexible, sessional academic work. Apply now to grow your clinical teaching   expertise   while guiding safe, evidence-based dental care for diverse patients       The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to   benefit   society through the transformative impact of education and research.   Discover more via our website.   Your next career opportunity     You will play a key role in developing   dental and oral health therapy   students’ clinical competence and professional judgement.   You will supervise preclinical and clinical activities at   the   Melbourne Dental School , guiding safe, high-quality care for diverse patients.   You will also build your own teaching skills within a collaborative,   values -driven dental school community.     What you will deliver:     Prepare for preclinical and clinical teaching sessions, reviewing materials, patient   records   and   logistics   to support   evidence based   learning.   Supervise,   guide   and educate   students during preclinical and clinical sessions, focusing on skills acquisition and knowledge application.   Review and approve patient dental records and   clinic    documentation , ensuring   accurate , compliant clinical records for every session.   Facilitate student feedback discussions and complete required assessment, marking,   questionnaires   and sessional administrative documentation.   Participate in meetings,   training   and compliance activities to   maintain   credentialing, child   safety   and high-quality teaching standards.     You may be a great fit   if   you :     Hold a primary dental qualification, eligible for registration with the Dental Board of Australia.   Bring at least   two   years’ clinical experience   (varies between programs) , with strong, contemporary evidence-based dental practice skills.   Maintain current   Ahpra   registration with no conditions, and   clinic   credentialing   appropriate to   clinical teaching   on the MDS teaching clinics. Demonstrate strong motivation to develop excellence in dental education,   assessment   and student feedback.   Work effectively both independently and collaboratively, contributing positively to diverse students,   patients   and academic colleagues.   Exhibit well-developed communication and interpersonal skills, supporting students’ learning in complex preclinical and clinical environments.   For further   information   please refer to the attached   job duties   description .       Your new team –   Melbourne Dental School   At the Melbourne Dental School, you will join a values-driven community within the Faculty of Medicine, Dentistry and Health Sciences. The   School   partners closely with the Royal Dental Hospital of Melbourne   (RDHM) , delivering high-impact clinical education and patient care. You will collaborate with skilled clinicians and educators who champion evidence-based practice,   innovation   and student success, while enjoying   strong support   for your professional development and wellbeing.     Be   y ourself     The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe   organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.   Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at UniMelb.   We're   committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.   Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process .   Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander   a pplicants     We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians.   Visit   our   Indigenous staff page   to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.           Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with our Indigenous Employment & Development team at   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au .     Application essentials:   Visit   \"apply with us\"   to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.   You must have current valid work rights for Australia. Visa sponsorship is not available for this role.   A Working with Children Check is   required   for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.    Please upload your resume and a cover letter outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.  Want to know more?   For queries related to this specific position, contact   mds-operations@unimelb.edu.au     For questions related to our recruitment process email   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at   hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au   (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').     Apply   today, and   join a community   that’s   shaping the future.   Job Duties Description – Doctor of Dental Surgery (DDS).pdf Job   Duties   Description – Bachelor of Oral Health   (BOH)   ( Coming   Soon)   Job   Duties   Description – Doctor of   Clinical   Dentistry   (DCD)   ( Coming   soon )"
    },
    "https://unimelb.wd105.myworkdayjobs.com/UoM_External_Career/job/Parkville-Victoria/Research-Assistant-in-Computational-Drug-Discovery_JR-016831-2": {
      "title": "Research Assistant in Computational Drug Discovery",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nRole type:  Full Time   (1.0 FTE) ; Fixed term for 2 years     Faculty:  Faculty of Science    School:   School of   BioSciences     Salary:  Level A :   $87,266 - $118,416   p.a.   plus 17% super     Innovative computational contraceptive research / high-impact women’s and reproductive health focus / supportive, interdisciplinary   BioSciences   environment   Apply now to drive data-rich contraception discovery and build your computational biology research career in a leading lab.   Investing in   you   – 17% superannuation, benefits package including salary packaging, health and wellbeing programs, discounted services, and professional development opportunities.      The University of Melbourne     We take pride in our people, who all contribute to our mission to  benefit  society through the transformative impact of education and research.  Discover more via our website.     Your next career opportunity       In this role you will lead computational analyses for a collaborative contraceptive discovery project.   You will apply ‘omics analysis, molecular   simulations   and machine learning to   identify   promising novel contraceptive candidates.   You will strengthen your HPC and pipeline skills while advancing impactful reproductive and women’s health research.   What   you will   deliver:       Lead computational analyses of large ‘omics datasets, including single-cell, spatial transcriptomic, proteomic and metabolomic data.   Implement and optimise molecular docking, molecular dynamics simulations and protein modelling approaches for contraceptive candidate discovery.   Develop,   document   and share reproducible, version-controlled analysis pipelines and notebooks using R, Python,   Bash   and HPC.   Prepare high-quality figures, reports, manuscripts and datasets for collaborators, funders, public   repositories   and high-impact journals.   Contribute to student mentoring, research proposals,   seminars   and School activities that promote diversity,   inclusion   and engagement.   You may be a great fit if you:       Hold or are near completing a PhD in computational biology, computer science, data   science   or related field.   Demonstrate strong R and/or Python skills, including experience with leading single-cell and bulk RNA-seq tools.   Apply robust statistical and machine learning methods to high-dimensional data, ensuring sound modelling,   normalisation   and testing.   Use HPC environments, Bash   scripting   and version control to deliver efficient, reproducible computational workflows.   Show evidence of research productivity through publications,   preprints   or significant open-source software contributions.   Bring enthusiasm for reproductive and women’s health and readiness to collaborate across multidisciplinary teams.   For further information, please refer to the attached PD.       What we offer you!       We offer the opportunity to be part of a vibrant community and enjoy a comprehensive range of benefits to support your success and sense of fulfilment, including:      Build future financial security with 17% superannuation     Supportive flexible work arrangements underpinned by our commitment to inclusion and well-being      Career development opportunities, including access to a range of tailored programs, such as Academic Women in Leadership, and learning platforms including LinkedIn Learning     Progressive, considerate leave provisions to empower your work-life balance and well-being, including leading parental leave, gender affirmation leave and cultural leave     Salary packaging and access to a range of discounted services including Bupa health insurance, and access to unique cultural and recreational benefits such as discounts for the Melbourne Theatre Company      Health and well-being services including a leading Employee Assistance Program      For more information check out our benefits page!      Your new team     You will join the School of  BioSciences , a vibrant community tackling global biological challenges from reproductive health to climate change. Working within the Faculty of Science, you will collaborate with experts in genomics, data  science  and molecular   biology. The  School  offers outstanding facilities, diverse  partnerships  and a supportive culture that values curiosity,  inclusion  and career development.     Be Yourself       The University of Melbourne is an Equal Opportunity Employer and a child-safe  organisation . The diversity of our community enriches us all, and we are committed to creating an inclusive and fair workplace where everyone is valued, respected, and empowered to succeed. We welcome applicants from all backgrounds, identities, and experiences.  Discover more about Diversity and Inclusion at   UniMelb .     We're  committed to a barrier-free recruitment process and ongoing workplace support, providing adjustments throughout. We warmly encourage applications from people with disabilities.  Learn more about how we support an accessible recruitment process.     Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Applicants       We aspire to be the University of choice for Indigenous Australians. Visit  our   Indigenous staff page  to learn more about our investment and support for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander staff.      Indigenous applicants are encouraged to connect with Korin  Korin , our Indigenous Employment and Development team, via   korin-korin@unimelb.edu.au     Application essentials:     Visit  \"apply with us\"  to learn more about the process, including tips and FAQs.     This role is eligible for visa   sponsorship   and we welcome international applicants. If successful, we will support you through this process.    A Working with Children Check is  required  for all positions. If successful, we will guide you through the process and reimburse you.      Please upload your  resume and a cover letter  outlining your interest and experience as part of the application process.     Please upload a  separate document addressing the Selection Criteria  outlined in the Position Description.         Want to know more?     For queries related to this specific position, contact Brittany Goods via email at  britt.goods@unimelb.edu.au       For questions related to our recruitment process email Oliver Bukasa at  hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au     For recruitment adjustments contact Kim Groizard on +61 3 9035 3218 or at  hr-careers@unimelb.edu.au  (subject: 'Recruitment Adjustments').      Apply  today, and  join a community  that’s  shaping the future.     Applications close:   18   September 2026   at  11:55 PM; Melbourne time zone.      Position Description:     JR-016831 - Research Assistant in Computational Drug Discovery - PD.docx JR-016831 - Research Assistant in Computational Drug Discovery - PD.pdf"
    },
